tory Home Career & Leadership Development Career & Leadership Development Student Life Career Development & Student Success Career & Leadership Development September 20, 2023 2026-05-11 11:04 We help you succeed at TWU and prepare you for life beyond graduation! The Office of Career Development is designed to cultivate an environment where students feel inspired and empowered to transform the world through comprehensive innovation, connections, and community. The Office of Career Development supports students and alumni while preparing for post-graduate academic and employment to: Advance equity and access to career resources Support diverse aspirations Encourage the pursuit of meaningful careers Want to stay up to date with the exciting and fun events hosted by the Career Development team? Follow us on Instagram! Instagram Career Services Career Services supports students through all stages of their college experience, from the first year through graduation. In this office, you can find resources and information that will help you gain relevant and practical career readiness through education and experiential learning within career counseling, part-time jobs, graduate school, and full-time employment. Housed in the Mosher Success center, the Career Development team is available to assist you! Appointments are recommended but walk-ins are welcome. As part of the TWU family, you'll receive an education similar to that of larger universities but at a fraction of the cost. Our instructors provide nurturing environments that cater to our students' needs. (423) 745-7504 204 E College Street Athens, TN 37303 Fax: (423) 744-9968 Navigation About Admissions Tuition & Aid Academics Athletics Student Life Alumni Quick Links Campus Directory How To Apply Bookstore | TWU Apparel & Merch Visit Campus Library Transcript Request myPortal Canvas Email Employment Opportunities Consumer Information TITLE IX | CARES ACT FUNDS | PRIVACY POLICY | HAZING POLICY All Rights Reserved © 2026